@startuml D3_Flow5_PlanMode_SDK_CICD
' ============================================================
' DOMAIN 3 — FLOW 5: Plan Mode + Iteration + Agent SDK + CI/CD
' (Topics 19–20, 24–25)
' CORE IDEAS:
'  * Plan mode = read-only THINK phase -> approval gate -> execute.
'  * SDK vs API: SDK = full AGENT LOOP; API = single completion.
'  * CI/CD: the -p flag = non-interactive; forget it -> job HANGS.
' ============================================================
title Domain 3 · Flow 5 — Plan Mode, Agent SDK & CI/CD (T19–20, 24–25)\n(Think->approve->execute · SDK=agent loop vs API=one call · -p or it hangs)

skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF6CC

start

' ---------- TOPIC 19–20: PLAN MODE ----------
partition "T19 · Plan Mode (separate THINKING from DOING)" {
  :Enter plan mode;
  note right
    Two entry paths (both just set the permission mode):
    * shift+tab cycles default -> accept edits -> PLAN
      (whole session STAYS in plan until you cycle out)
    * `/plan` prefix on ONE request, then returns to prior mode
    Plan mode = a PERMISSION MODE, not a separate tool.
  end note
  #LightCyan:Read-only: reads relevant files, reasons, produces a PROPOSAL;
  note right
    A well-formed plan has 3 parts:
    1. ORDERED numbered steps (not a paragraph of intentions)
    2. FILES TOUCHED — every file named explicitly
    3. RISKS / assumptions called out
    Missing any -> push back before approving.
    e.g. "rename User->Account": step1 edit models/user.ts;
    step2 update 15 named imports; step3 run tests;
    risk: assuming type unused in mobile package.
  end note
}

partition "T19–20 · The Approval Gate (primary quality checkpoint)" {
  if (Read the plan critically — approve, edit, or reject?) then (APPROVE)
    #LightGreen:Session EXITS plan mode -> executes in the chosen mode;
    note left
      Check before approving: scope matches intent?
      file paths correct for real layout? risks you can
      resolve from domain knowledge? Approving WITHOUT reading
      defeats the whole purpose ("fast is fine, absent isn't").
    end note
  elseif (EDIT) then
    #LightYellow:Trim scope / reorder / add a step, THEN approve;
    note right
      Editing is faster than a full re-plan. Claude executes
      YOUR version, not the original.
    end note
  else (REJECT)
    #Pink:Restate intent more precisely -> re-plan;
  endif
  :During execution, if an assumption BREAKS -> RE-PLAN;
  note right
    Re-plan trigger: expected file missing / codebase assumption
    wrong. If it breaks only ONE step -> patch & proceed; if it
    undermines downstream steps -> re-plan.
    FAILURE MODE: silent improvisation — Claude adapts around an
    unexpected state instead of surfacing it. FIX (behavioural):
    "if anything contradicts the plan, pause and tell me first."
    Habits: short plans (5-8 steps), named files, explicit risks.
  end note
  #LightBlue:WHEN to plan: cross-file refactors · schema/API changes · ambiguous asks;
  note right
    Skip it for a single mechanical fix / typo / instantly
    reversible REPL work. Heuristic: undo in 10s -> skip;
    30 min to unwind -> plan first.
    Pairing: subagent investigates -> main agent plans ->
    hook validates -> staged human review.
  end note
}

' ---------- TOPIC 24: AGENT SDK ----------
partition "T24 · The Claude Agent SDK (was: Claude Code SDK)" {
  :Import the SDK into your OWN program;
  note right
    Same Claude Code capabilities as the CLI, but YOUR CODE
    drives instead of a human. Call methods to start sessions,
    pass prompts as strings, stream output + tool events.
    Configure at creation: model, tool categories, working dir,
    env vars, system prompt; inject file contents; set tool
    permissions; append follow-up prompts mid-session.
    Use case: a bot opens a session when a PR lands, streams the
    review, posts it as a GitHub comment — no human typing.
  end note
  if (Do you need the full AGENT LOOP?) then (YES)
    #LightGreen:Use the SDK;
    note right
      SDK = manages the whole loop: multi-step tool use, file
      edits, shell commands, streaming. One prompt -> it handles
      everything in between + real-time observability.
    end note
  else (NO — one model call)
    #LightYellow:Use the direct API;
    note right
      Direct API = prompt in, completion out. No session state,
      no tool orchestration unless you build it. Also choose the
      API if you're building your OWN agent framework.
    end note
  endif
}

' ---------- TOPIC 25: CI/CD ----------
partition "T25 · Claude Code in CI/CD (the -p flag)" {
  if (Is a human present to answer prompts?) then (NO — automated pipeline)
    #LightGreen:Pass the -p flag (print / non-interactive mode);
    note right
      -p = one-shot: take prompt, run the FULL agentic loop
      non-interactively, print result to stdout, exit with a
      status code. Companions: --output-format json (parseable),
      stream-json (live events), --allowed-tools (scope),
      --resume / --continue (build on a past session).
      Contract: stdout = result; exit 0 = success, non-zero = fail.
    end note
  else (YES — workstation)
    #LightYellow:Interactive mode (default REPL) — mutually exclusive with -p;
  endif
  #Pink:FORGET -p -> Claude opens an interactive session and WAITS\n-> the job HANGS, burns runner minutes, times out;
  note right
    == STRUCTURING AUTOMATED TASKS (4 principles) ==
    1. ATOMIC — one task, one outcome (don't lint + doc in one call)
    2. SELF-CONTAINED — no memory of previous runs; include context
    3. STRUCTURED OUTPUT (JSON) — next step parses, not text-scrapes
    4. IDEMPOTENT — pipelines retry; same run -> same result
    ----
    GitHub: use the OFFICIAL Claude Code action (install-github-app)
    — trigger by mentioning @claude in an issue/PR. Store the API
    key as a GitHub Actions SECRET. A raw `claude -p` step is just
    generic SDK automation, NOT the documented integration.
    SECURITY: minimum necessary permissions — unattended runs mean
    narrow scope limits blast radius. Always set a step TIMEOUT.
  end note
}

stop

floating note left
  == FLOW 5 SPINE ==
  Plan mode = read-only THINK -> approval gate (approve/edit/reject)
  -> execute, re-plan if assumptions break.
  SDK drives the AGENT LOOP from code; API = a single completion.
  CI/CD needs -p (non-interactive) or the job hangs.
  ----
  == HIGH-YIELD FACTS ==
  * Plan mode IS a permission mode (shift+tab / --permission-mode plan)
  * Good plan = ordered steps + named files + explicit risks
  * Undo in 10s -> skip planning; 30 min -> plan
  * SDK = full agent loop + streaming; API = one call, no session
  * "Agent SDK" was formerly "Claude Code SDK"
  * -p = print/non-interactive; forget it -> HANG
  * atomic · self-contained · JSON output · idempotent
  * GitHub -> official action + API key as a secret
end note

@enduml
